==========================================================================================
(A) FIXED-JET DOUBLE WELL V_w=(w^2/2)((y/w)^2-1)^2 : jets at critical points fixed in w,
    barrier height w^2/2 -> inf, lambda_1 -> 0  [T]+[V]
      w    V''(barrier)   V''(well)   V''''(barrier)   barrier   lambda_1(FEM)   e^{-barrier}
     1.0     -2.0000      +4.0064      1.2000e+01       0.500     8.997e-01     6.07e-01
     1.5     -2.0000      +3.9936      5.3333e+00       1.125     3.188e-01     3.25e-01
     2.0     -2.0000      +4.0064      3.0000e+00       2.000     1.137e-01     1.35e-01
     3.0     -2.0000      +3.9936      1.3333e+00       4.500     9.089e-03     1.11e-02
     4.0     -2.0000      +4.0064      7.5000e-01       8.000     2.859e-04     3.35e-04
    => V''(0)=-2 and V''(well)=+4 are INDEPENDENT of w; V''''->0. The full critical-point
       jet converges, yet lambda_1->0. NO criterion f(V'',V''',V'''',...) of the critical-
       point jets can give a uniform floor: the gap is the NONLOCAL barrier action.
==========================================================================================
(B) 4-CONVEX family V_g=(g/2)(x^2-1)^2 : V''''=6g>0 everywhere, kappa_a=V''+a V'''' at
    the barrier = (6a-2)g > 0 for a>1/3, yet lambda_1 -> 0 (Kramers)  [T]+[V]
       g    V''''=6g    V''(barrier)  kappa_1/3(bar)  kappa_1(bar)   lambda_1(FEM)
     0.5       3.000      -0.500         +0.500        +2.500     7.921e-01
     1.0       6.000      -1.000         +1.000        +5.000     8.459e-01
     2.0      12.000      -2.000         +2.000       +10.000     7.487e-01
     4.0      24.000      -4.000         +4.000       +20.000     4.545e-01
     8.0      48.000      -8.000         +8.000       +40.000     1.191e-01
    16.0      96.000     -16.000        +16.000       +80.000     4.575e-03
    => 'higher-order log-concavity' (V''''>=0) and the regularized curvature are SATISFIED
       (kappa_1=+4g at the barrier) while the gap collapses. A higher-derivative criterion
       positive on the double well cannot imply a Poincare bound.  [NG]
==========================================================================================
(C) FREE FIELD V=1/2 k^2 x^2 : all jets of order >=3 vanish; lambda_1=k^2 -> 0  [T]+[V]
    k= 1.00: V''=k^2=  1.0000  V''''=0  lambda_1(FEM)=0.99999   (ACID PASS)
    k= 0.50: V''=k^2=  0.2500  V''''=0  lambda_1(FEM)=0.25000   (ACID PASS)
    k= 0.10: V''=k^2=  0.0100  V''''=0  lambda_1(FEM)=0.01000   (ACID PASS)
    k= 0.02: V''=k^2=  0.0004  V''''=0  lambda_1(FEM)=0.00040   (ACID PASS)
    => every higher-order criterion that is a function of the jet returns 0 on the free
       field (all higher jets are exactly 0). No false floor is manufactured.
==========================================================================================
(D) EXACT ONE-PLAQUETTE SU(2), theta=pi, G''(0)=A-B beta^2, A=0.20511530 B=0.01105929,
    beta*=4.30661  [T]+[V]
     beta   G''(0)     A-B b^2    G''''(0)   kappa1=G''+G''''  lambda_1   h^2/4    gate
     2.50   +0.13599   +0.13599    +0.0964     +0.2324           0.3398    0.0944   -1.92
     5.00   -0.07137   -0.07137    +0.3312     +0.2598           0.4139    0.1970   -2.50
    10.00   -0.90081   -0.90081    +1.5205     +0.6197           0.4042    0.4022   -2.82
    Below beta* the barrier has G''>0 (log-concave): plain BE works.
    Above beta* G''(0)<0 but the exact marginal gap stays O(0.4): it is a compact tilted
    SINGLE well, the G''<0 point is an off-mass shoulder (Q3), not a bottleneck.  Note
    kappa1=G''+G''''=+0.62 > lambda_1=0.40 at beta=10 (and >lambda_1 everywhere above),
    so the 'regularized curvature' is NOT a lower bound for lambda_1 on the exact model [NG].
