(F) NONLOCAL: the only functional controlling lambda_1 is the Cheeger/gate capacity h(nu).
    On V=(g/2)(x^2-1)^2 the gate density rho(gate)~e^{-DeltaV} and h~rho(gate)/mass:  [T]+[V]
       g    rho(gate)     Cheeger h    h^2/4      lambda_1     H1?
     0.5   2.561e-01    5.122e-01   6.56e-02   7.921e-01   gate-bound = H1
     2.0   1.864e-01    3.728e-01   3.47e-02   7.487e-01   gate-bound = H1
     8.0   1.932e-02    3.865e-02   3.73e-04   1.191e-01   gate-bound = H1
    16.0   5.207e-04    1.041e-03   2.71e-07   4.575e-03   gate-bound = H1
    => h is a NONLOCAL (barrier-action) functional; h>=h0 <=> rho(gate)>=c <=> no interior
       barrier <=> H1. The nonlocal rescue IS H1. Nonlocal Gamma / fractional LSI still
       require a pointwise curvature floor (absent). Orderless quotient: half-line optimality
       of 1-D Cheeger has no analogue on A/G; only the tautology lambda_1>=h^2/4 survives.
==========================================================================================
SUMMARY (no QED):  (A) fixed critical-point jet + lambda_1->0 => no local high-jet criterion;
  (B) 4-convex / regularized curvature positive but gap 0 => [NG] higher-order log-concavity;
  (C) free field acid pass; (D) one-plaquette: barrier G''=A-Bb^2<0 past beta*=4.30661;
  (E) 1D SU(2) finite chi via plain BE; (F) the only working nonlocal functional = Cheeger
  gate = H1. Uniform bound still [O]=H1. Clay 0%.
